From 34b0179602bba709ea9e96a0a4b7494108771063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:44:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq5018: don't propagate ubi0_axi_clk_src rate
 changes to GPLL0

ubi0_axi_clk_src has CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, but its parents are XO and the
read-only GPLL0/GPLL2 post-dividers, so propagating can never change their
rate. It does make the clock core treat any rounding gap as a GPLL0 rate
change: setting 400 MHz (GPLL0 / 2) while GPLL0 reads back 799999998 Hz
makes GPLL0 the top of the change, and clk_change_rate() then re-runs
set_rate on every GPLL0 consumer - the live NoCs and, gated at that
moment, sdcc1_apps_clk_src, which fails with "rcg didn't update its
configuration" and leaves the eMMC controller and board hung. The NSS
driver sets exactly this rate when it starts the UBI32 core.

Fixes: e3fdbef1bab8 ("clk: qcom: Add Global Clock controller (GCC) driver for IPQ5018")
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
index dfc587d8c..28afbc462 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq5018.c
@@ -1197,7 +1197,6 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 ubi0_axi_clk_src = {
 		.parent_data = gcc_xo_gpll0_gpll2,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(gcc_xo_gpll0_gpll2),
 		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 	},
 };
 
